    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has many unused imports and unused data provider methods (`data_samples`, `data_badDates`, etc.) that belong to a larger test class but are orphaned here. I'll clean those up and reformat the dense, wall-of-text data to improve readability.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and orphaned data provider methods, splits the long `INSTANCE` initializer across readable lines, introduces a named `INSTANCE_YEAR_STARTS` constant to make the two chronology variants self-documenting, and extracts shared expected-string prefixes into named constants so each test-case row clearly shows only the date and the discriminating suffix."
    }
